---
import Guide from '../layouts/Guide.astro';
import VersionNotice from '../components/VersionNotice.astro';
import { release, releaseURL, download, source } from '../data/site';
---
<Guide title="Releases & evidence" description="Version-pinned downloads, public qualification records, and explicit limits on what has been verified." sections={[{id:'current',label:'Current release'},{id:'qualification',label:'Qualification'},{id:'provenance',label:'Checksums & provenance'},{id:'history',label:'Release history'}]}>
  <h2 id="current">Livewire v{release.version} <span class="status-tag">PUBLISHED</span></h2><p>Install from the published GitHub release. The website keeps version, download names, and command examples together so instructions can be checked against the binary you run.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={releaseURL}>Open release <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/install/">Installation guide →</a></div><VersionNotice />
  <h2 id="qualification">A reproducible evidence trail</h2><p>Qualification binds the tested source digest and binary hashes to CLI reports, independently observed traffic, repeated runs, and cleanup records. Read the report for the exact version and platform instead of treating one successful exchange as universal support.</p><ul><li>Automated application and packet checks exercise the actual built CLI.</li><li>Long-running software-lab runs distinguish checked responses from unverified frame transmission.</li><li>Release rebuilds compare artifact bytes, checksum manifests, and the frozen binary hashes.</li><li>Physical NIC/device behavior and native ARM64 execution remain separate qualification work.</li></ul><p><a class="text-link" href={source(release.qualificationPath)}>Read v{release.version} qualification <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
  <h2 id="provenance">Verify the artifact you downloaded</h2><div class="download-list"><a class="download-item" href={download('SHA256SUMS')}><div><strong>SHA-256 manifest</strong><small>SHA256SUMS</small></div><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="download-item" href={download(`livewire-${release.version}.cdx.json`)}><div><strong>Software bill of materials</strong><small>CycloneDX dependency inventory</small></div><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div><p>GitHub artifact attestations bind build artifacts to their repository workflow. Follow the <a href="/install/#verify">verification steps</a> before running a downloaded binary.</p>
  <h2 id="history">Prior releases remain identifiable</h2><p>Older version tags and their evidence stay available. When command meanings change, read the migration notes before updating scripts.</p><p><a href={`${release.repository}/releases`}>All GitHub releases ↗</a> · <a href={source('CHANGELOG.md')}>Changelog ↗</a></p>
</Guide>
